<?xml version="1.0" ?>

<!-- acousticDamper.xml
acousticDamper is a method to introduce a viscous term specifically conceived to reduce the
amount of acoustic pressure waves in weakly-compressible SPH models. It is based in the
formulation presented in:
    P.N Sun, C. Pilloton, M. Antuono, A. Colagrossi "Inclusion of an acoustic damper term in weakly-compressible SPH models"
    Journal of Computational Physics, Volume 483, 2023, 112056, ISSN 0021-9991, https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jcp.2023.112056.

This term only acts on the acoustic component of the pressure field, which is
generated as a consequence of liquid impacts and of the assumption that the ﬂuid is
weakly-compressible, whereas it leaves the incompressible-like component unchanged.

The proposed acoustic damper term converges to zero when the
particle resolution increases, recovering the consistency with the Navier-Stokes equations.

Remember that after including this preset, a new property alpha_ad should be set as a general variable, while a new value of lambda_ad should be imposed
for each particles set. Nonetheless, these two parameters are related through the relationship:

  lambda_ad = alpha_ad * refd * cs * hfac * dr

-->

<sphInput>
    <Variables>
        <Variable name="alpha_ad" type="float" value="0.0" />
        <Variable name="lambda_ad" type="float*" length="n_sets" />
        <Variable name="fi_ad" type="vec*" length="N" />
    </Variables>
    <Tools>
		    <Tool action="insert" after="Sort" type="set" name="cfd Reinit fi_ad" in="fi_ad" value="VEC_ZERO"/>
        <Tool name="cfd acoustic damper interactions" action="insert" after="cfd interactions" type="kernel" entry_point="acousticTerm" path="../../Scripts/cfd/acousticDamper.cl" />
        <Tool name="cfd acoustic damper rates" action="insert" after="cfd rates" type="kernel" entry_point="rates" path="../../Scripts/cfd/acousticDamper.cl" />
 	</Tools>
</sphInput>
